MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I noticed this too, but for me it's a bit shorter than several minutes and occasional. I haven't been able to get to the bottom of it and I thought it was OS X only as I've never noticed it on linux. Feel free to open an issue about it, that's helpful to gather information on the problem anyway, but I don't have a solution at the moment. If your problem is reproducible, then there is an obvious theory about what is going on which is saving you current environment. If you have a lot of data in your current environment, that could be it. gc() will tell you how much space your session is allocating (and trigger garbage collection). Try to run R --vanilla and repro your problem from there, that will give us some additional info.

Antonio

