A short update on this issue: turns out that the following command retrieves only a single output file when there are more than one (which probably maps to having more than one reducer):

$ hadoop dfs -text /user/cloudera/IO_test/IOtest_1340820605.csv/part* > IOtest_1340820605.csv

My current guess is that it can be fixed by using 'append' (>>) instead of 'overwrite' (>)

$ hadoop dfs -text /user/cloudera/IO_test/IOtest_1340820605.csv/part* >> IOtest_1340820605.csv

Alternative ideas would be appreciated...

-Saar

